--- kps-S31ag interpretation (handoff A) ---
EXACT BOUND: any covering set with apex a=14V has largest RAW lonely arc <= 6/(7a) = 3/(49V),
because the apex's own danger comb (width 1/(7a), spacing 1/a) leaves arcs <= (1-1/7)/a.
=> the RAW direct arc is NOT bounded below; it decays as 3/(49V), uniformly across all 4 families.
Raw-arc crossover (arc passes l_core~0.0045) = V ~ 3/(49*0.0045) ~ 14-15 (CONFIRMED uniform above).
This is a DIFFERENT, much smaller constant than the witness-route V* atlas (~234): RAW vs NORMALIZED.
mac-mini-S61's "bounded ~0.005 to V*~200" must be the NORMALIZED/peeled arc; the raw arc fails at ~15.
The peeling/normalization (Node-3) IS the reduction from the failed raw arc to the witness object.
